Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.50,0:00:09.50,TitleJa,,0,0,0,,{\pos(960,575)}父からの小さな贈り物
Dialogue: 2,0:00:11.26,0:01:40.02,Header,,0,0,0,,H004  •  第4文型 [SVOO]
Dialogue: 2,0:00:11.26,0:00:15.46,English,,0,0,0,,My father gave me a small box.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:15.46,0:00:19.90,English,,0,0,0,,Inside were old photographs and one letter.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:21.76,0:00:25.30,English,,0,0,0,,He had kept them safe for a long time.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:25.30,0:00:33.06,English,,0,0,0,,In one photo, my young father smiled next to my grandfather.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:34.38,0:00:39.02,English,,0,0,0,,This is my childhood, he whispered softly.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:39.64,0:00:45.74,English,,0,0,0,,I came to see the ordinary box as something precious.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:47.04,0:00:56.14,English,,0,0,0,,I had never imagined that a piece of paper could carry such worth.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:58.28,0:01:09.42,English,,0,0,0,,Father taught me about the bonds and affection within a family, not with words, but quietly.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:11.34,0:01:14.42,English,,0,0,0,,The photograph gave me comfort.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:14.42,0:01:25.22,English,,0,0,0,,He said, I give you this, and the small gift carried years of respect and memory.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:25.22,0:01:31.70,English,,0,0,0,,I nodded to my father and accepted the box.
Dialogue: 2,0:01:31.70,0:01:39.82,English,,0,0,0,,A gentle desire to give something back grew in my heart.
